commits.message:
Replace native `if` in prototype kit init.scss

Import `govuk-if` explicitly as the value is used as a default for
the variable, which would require a fair bit more code:

```scss
// This needs to be outside any at rule to be in the global scope
$govuk-assets-path: null !default;
@if $govuk-assets-path != null {
  @if ($govuk-prototype-kit-major-version > 12) {
    $govuk-assets-path: $govuk-extensions-url-context + "/govuk-frontend/dist/govuk/assets/"
  } @else {
    $govuk-assets-path: "/govuk/assets/"
  }
}
```

Add import only file for `index.scss`

The file needs not only to `@forward` index, but also resolve `$govuk-font-url-function` and `$govuk-image-url-function` into Sass functions if they're configured as strings.

We need to use and and or because we cannot use:

- `@if` because `@use` and `@forward` need to be the first rules loaded
- `govuk-if` as `meta.get-function` would run even if `$govuk-font-url-function` is not defined

The `@forward "settings"` will need to be in each import only file that includes font-url or image-url (ie. any file past the `tools` layer and the `tools/_index.scss` file.

- we can't load it with `@import` before `@forward`
- if we put it in a module `meta.get-function` wouldn't be able to get a reference to the function set as a string:

  ```scss
  // index.scss
  // defines the function and configures $govuk-font-url-function
  @function font-url() { /* creates the URL */ }
  $govuk-font-url-function: 'font-url';
  @import 'font-url';
  ```

  ```scss
  // font-url.import.scss
  // When `@import`ed from `index.scss`, it can access to both `$govuk-font-url-function`
  // and the `font-url` function
  @forward $govuk-font-url-function;
  ```

  ```scss
  // font-url.scss
  // The `!default` allows the value of `$govuk-font-url-function` to be set
  // however, because the file is included with `@forward` it cannot access
  // the `font-url` function, as it's not part of the module
  $govuk-font-url-function: null !default;
  ```
/* Use `$govuk-font-url-function` */
```

Make `$govuk-imported-modules` public

This will allow it to be shared when `@import`ing multiple files that use `govuk-exports`, for example:

```scss
@import "pkg:govuk-frontend/base";
@import "pkg:govuk-frontend/button";
@import "pkg:govuk-frontend/tags";
```

Include button config settings within base

Co-authored-by: Romaric Pascal <hello@romaricpascal.is>
Co-authored-by: Oliver Byford <36degrees@users.noreply.github.com>

- adjust the button mixin to be configurable
- have `base` forward/import the button settings so they're available for the user:

```CSS
@use "base" with (
  $govuk-button-background-colour: hotpink;
);

// Once base is configured, you can do any of the following to get the button with config:
@use "index";
@use "components";
@use "components/button";

This keeps all config in the same statement.

The `@import` path works the same as before"
